   "id": "b4",
   "function": "demonstration",
   "scene_type": "zlx_plug",
   "spoken": "High voltage makes a spark jump across the gap between two electrodes. And it had to be quick: according to Bosch, early engines ran at about a hundred revolutions per minute, car engines at up to a thousand. At a thousand rpm, each spark gets only a fraction of a second. Speed mattered from the very start.",
